      "message": "This is mostly always going to be the case, but there are corner cases where we could end up with a `fCurrentCommandBuffer` that is not null but haven\u0027t actually added any commands to it yet.  There is currently a debug-only `CommandBuffer::hasWork()` function is used to add an additional level of log warning when this is the case.  This situation only really comes up when the client inserts a recording or some other Context API that should result in work (hence we created the command buffer), but then that operation fails for some transient reason.\n\nI believe that is why we\u0027ve logged the two scenarios differently, because the first case (null fCurrentCommandBuffer) represents a case where the client could have tracked that it never did anything with the Context. The second case is more a warning that things are in an unexpected state but it would have been hard for the client to know about it.\n\nHowever, in either case, if the client is just relying on `hasPendingGPUWork()` to guard when they decide to call `submit()`, it seems like we should just fold that into the meaning of `hasPendignGPUWork()` and simplify the logging in `QueueManager::submitToGpu`.",
